{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793696005,"nonce":"dLPJgrnmxgVZ/gHqNEcVl3Ct0t8=","title":"Indeterminate progress bar and a Spinner under a Toast are not clipped","message":"Reported by the owner, 2026-11-03, in cn_demo. The indeterminate progress bar's pill is drawn outside its track: in the screenshot it sits over the text above the track (\"shadcn-inspired component library\") instead of staying inside the track's bounds. A Spinner shows a similar effect when it is under a Toast.\n\nNot investigated; these are only where to start.\n- crates/blinc_cn/src/components/progress.rs: the track is built with .overflow_clip() (line ~131) and the bar's motion is the `cn-progress-pulse` keyframes on `.cn-progress[data-indeterminate] \u003e .cn-progress-bar` (cn_styles.rs ~1012). The bar is animated by a CSS animation, so the first question is whether an animated child (its transform or translate) is still clipped by an overflow_clip parent; the layer promotion of animated nodes (compositor) is a candidate, since it paints a promoted subtree separately from its clipping ancestor.\n- Spinner (components/spinner.rs) rotates a bordered arc with a clip_path under a Toast; Toasts are foreground, overlay content, which points at the same promotion or foreground-layer path rather than at either widget.\n- Toast and overlay content paint on the foreground layer; a clip on an ancestor may not reach an animated or promoted descendant there.\n\nTo do: reproduce headless (blinc_recorder Headless: mount cn::progress_indeterminate() in a narrow track, advance the animation, check that no pixel outside the track is the bar's colour; likewise a spinner inside a toast), then find which clip is lost. Related: dac4f51 and 969d5aa (canvas and foreground paint order), 5bfc932-style compositor issues.","files":null}]}